      {
        "id": "post-rpm-massive-test-particle-action",
        "kind": "postulate",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Massive spinless test-particle action",
        "statement": "For a spinless, structureless massive test body of constant primitive mass $m>0$ on a prescribed background satisfying [[post-rpm-test-clock-and-background]], adopt the action\n\n$$S_m[x]=-mc\\int\\sqrt{-g(dx/ds,dx/ds)}\\,ds=-mc^2\\int d\\tau,$$\n\nfor future timelike curves, with fixed-endpoint stationary paths as the model's free trajectories. When $s$ is measured in seconds, $T$ has units metres per second; in SI units the action has units joule-seconds. The equality is the proper-time change of variable of [[thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization]]. This is an adopted model premise, not a consequence of the metric or clock postulate. It excludes self-gravity, radiation reaction, spin, finite-size structure, particle creation, and quantum effects; it does not assert empirical adequacy for any particular body.",
        "deps": [
          "post-rpm-test-clock-and-background",
          "thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "post-rpm-test-clock-and-background": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "thm-rpm-proper-time-parametrization": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "dependency_level": 2,
        "sources": {
          "references": [
