        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Flat local geometry without completeness",
        "statement": "For $L,\\ell>0$, consider the flat Lorentzian cylinder $M_L=(\\mathbb R/L\\mathbb Z)\\times\\mathbb R^3$ and the open slab $S_\\ell=(0,\\ell)\\times\\mathbb R^3$, each with metric $-d\\theta^2+\\sum_{i=1}^3d(x^i)^2$ and future direction $\\partial_\\theta$, where $d\\theta$ is induced by the covering coordinate on $\\mathbb R/L\\mathbb Z$. The cylinder contains a closed future timelike geodesic. The slab contains a timelike geodesic defined on a finite affine interval that cannot be extended inside the slab. Thus a locally Minkowski metric alone supplies neither chronology nor geodesic completeness.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-spacetime-observer-and-worldline"
        ],
